- Our stale pointer at the original offset will now point into the newly allocated object

Actually, there's an even better strategy. In glibc:
- When realloc shrinks a chunk significantly, it can split the chunk- The remainder becomes a free chunk
- We can then allocate a new object that takes over this free chunk

